@using NEM.Contracts

@* The weather basis changes how a storage or reliability result should be read, so it is stated
   on the page rather than left in provenance. The wording is the artifact's own. *@
<aside class="weather-basis" aria-label="Weather basis">
    <p class="weather-basis-label">@KindLabel(Basis.Kind)</p>
    <p class="weather-basis-location">@Basis.LocationName</p>
    <p class="weather-basis-description">@Basis.Description</p>
    <p class="weather-basis-source">@Basis.SourceFile</p>
    @* A dispatch result records one site per region, but a region's solar and wind traces can be
       assembled from different weather files — New South Wales draws solar from Dubbo and wind from
       Armidale, roughly 300km apart. The site named above is therefore the run's stated basis
       rather than necessarily the only location behind it, and saying so is the difference between
       incomplete provenance and wrong provenance. The weather inputs page reads the weather
       artifact directly and names the site behind each role. *@
    <p class="weather-basis-caveat">
        One site is recorded per region here. Solar and wind traces may come from different weather
        files, so this names the run's stated basis rather than every location behind it.
        <a href="inputs/weather">See the site behind each role</a>.
    </p>
</aside>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public WeatherBasisDTO Basis { get; set; } = default!;

    private static string KindLabel(WeatherBasisKind kind) => kind switch
    {
        WeatherBasisKind.TypicalMeteorologicalYear => "Weather basis · typical meteorological year",
        _ => "Weather basis",
    };
}
